caption: Complete Use Procedure
engine-rule: complete-use-procedure

### Every Word Tradition gives an ordered procedure that covers:

- Stating the intended effect and exact result.

- Selecting every required Word or syntactic element.

- Confirming that the expression is grammatical, unambiguous, and within scope.

- Determining effect class and all numerical parameters.

- Determining casting or construction time, practices, preparation, activation, and action economy.

- Calculating complexity, energy, Tally, material, HP, risk, stored value, or other costs.

- Determining every governing skill roll, sequence, modifier, required margin, and assistance rule.

- Resolving attacks, defenses, resistance, contests, transformations, partial expressions, and multiple targets.

- Resolving success, ordinary failure, partial success, critical results, interruption, maintenance, cancellation, countering, dispelling, and destruction of prepared media.

- Recording any continuing, stored, transferable, linked, enchanted, or otherwise persistent result.
